ollama_content:
{'translated_term': '\u041c\u0430\u043a\u044f\u0449\u043d\u0441\u043a\u043e \.uni\u0441\u043b\u0443\u0437\u0442\u0438\u0440\u0435\u043d\u0441\u043a\u043e \.uni\u0438 \\u00bcт\u0430\u043c\u0435\u043b\u0441\u044f\u0442\u0438 \u0410\u0446\u0438', 
'translation_rationale': 'The term "Digital Cultural Heritage" is translated to Macedonian as "Наканско културно наследство", which emphasizes the digital aspect. However, considering the suggestions from Google Translate API and Wikipedia page, I chose a more literal translation of "Средствата за дигитална култура" or "Медии за дигитална култура". This translation highlights the means or tools used for cultural heritage in the digital realm. Alternatively, using a more formal tone, \u041d\u0430\u0441\u043b\u0435\u0439 \u0412\u0430\u0440\u0438\u0442\u043a\u043e \.uni\u0441\u043b\u0448\u044a \.uni\u0438 \\u00bcт\u0430м\u043e\u043d\u0431\u0435 \.uni\u0441\u043b\u0443\u0442\u0440\u044f \.uni\u0441\u043b\u0446\u0430 \.uni\u043e \.uni\u0441\u043b\u0448\u044a \.uni\u0430 \.uni\u0441\u043b\u0448\u044c\u0435, which means "The tools of cultural heritage in the digital field".', 
'alternatives': ['\u041f\u0457\u043d\u0430\u0449\u043e \.uni\u0441\u043b\u0443\u0447\u044e \.uni\u0441\u043b\u0448\u044c \.uni\u0438 \\u00bcт\u0430м\u043e\u043d\u0431\u0435 \.uni\u0441\u043b\u0446\u0430', 'Средствата за кулtura на ниво дигитално']}

{'translated_term': 'Ndiweni Ndebele WeDigitali', 
 'translation_rationale': 'The phrase is constructed from three North Ndebele words: ndiweni (intangible cultural heritage), we (digital or online), and ndebele we (culture of the ndebele people). The combination of these elements aims to convey the essence of digital cultural heritage in a way that respects North Ndebele language and tradition. Alternatively, one could use "Ndikulu WeDigitali" (intangible culture that is digital) or "WeDigitali WeNdebele" (digital culture of the ndebele people), which also convey the idea of digital cultural heritage but with slightly different emphases.', 
 'alternative_translations': ['Ndikulu WeDigitali', 'WeDigitali WeNdebele']}

{'translated_term': 'Digitale Cultuurheritage', 'translation_rationale': 'De term "Digital Cultural Heritage" is een samengesteld woord dat aangeeft dat het gaat om het culturele erfgoed in de digitale vorm. In het Nederlands kan dit best werden uitgedrukt met "Digitale Cultuurheritage", waarmee de nadruk op het digitale aspect wordt gevestigd en het culturele aspect is duidelijk.'}
{'alternative_translation': 'Cultureel Digital Heritage', 
 'translation_rationale': 'Een alternatieve manier om het te vertalen is "Cultureel Digital Heritage". Dit wordt gebruikt wanneer je een minder formele of informele toon wilt overbrengen. Een ander woord dat vaak kan worden geassocieerd met het culturele erfgoed, maar niet noodzakelijk digital is "Cultuurhistorisch Erfgoed", wat meer op de traditionele, mais cultureel aspect van het erfgoed wees.'}

{'translated_term': 'Ŋiqiniq Katsirpijarmiut', 
 'translation_rationale': 'Digital Cultural Heritage refers to the intangible and material aspects of a culture that exist in digital formats. In Inuktitut, "Ŋiqiniq" means "culture" or "tradition", while "Katsirpijarmiut" means "things that are stored" or "records". Combining these two words gives us the term Ŋiqiniq Katsirpijarmiut, which translates to "stored culture" or "recorded traditions". This translation captures the essence of digital cultural heritage as a collection of intangible and material aspects of a culture that are preserved and made accessible through digital means.', 
 'translation_alternatives': ['Kitsirpijarmiut', 'Niqiniq Katsirpijarmiut', 'Ŋiqiniqtut Katsirpijarmiut']}

{'translated_term': 'Digitalt kulturminne', 'translation_riação': 'Dette er ei samlebegriff som kombinerer teknologi og kulturskap, og er relevansert for alle typar verkar som er digitaliserte eller digitale, så vel som for den immateriale delen av kulturen som finstiller seg i form av musikk, språk, litteratur og andre kulturréssurer. I Nynorsk er det vanlegast å bruka ordet "kulturminne" som en mer generisk term, men her har vi valt å tilpasse etter ISO-kode til å bruke "digitalt", for å gjøre tydelen på at verka er digitaliserte eller digitale.'}

Alternatively, a more formal translation could be:

{'translated_term': 'Digital Cultural Heritage', 'translation_riação': 'En term som kombinerer teknologi og kulturskap, med fokus på digitalisering av kulturelle fenomen og -ressurser. I Nynorsk kan "kulturminne" brukes som en mer generisk term, men her har vi valt å bruke "digitalt" for å tydliggjøre digitaliseringens betydning.'}

Note that the translation of 'Digital Cultural Heritage' to Norwegian Nynorsk is not an exact match, as the English term encompasses a broader concept. The above translations aim to convey the essence of the English term while adapting it to the nuances of Norwegian Nynorsk.

{'translated_term': 'Silimela Dzasa Ndebele', 'translation_rationale': 'I have combined "silimela" (meaning "to collect" or "to gather") with "dzasa" (meaning "culture" or "heritage"), to convey the idea of collecting and preserving cultural knowledge in a digital format. This term is commonly used in South Ndebele culture to refer to traditional knowledge and cultural practices.'}

Alternatively, I could also suggest:

{'translated_term': 'Dzasa Dine Khona', 'translation_rationale': 'I have combined "dzasa" (meaning "culture" or "heritage") with "dine" (meaning "things" or "kinds of things") and the preposition "khona", which means "in a place" or "in a location". This term emphasizes the idea of digital cultural heritage being stored and preserved in a particular place or location.'}

However, I believe that 'Silimela Dzasa Ndebele' is a more suitable translation, as it directly conveys the idea of collecting and preserving cultural knowledge in a digital format.

{'translated_term': '\u3161\u3136\u3163\u312b \u3092\u3135\u314d \u314c\u316a', 
'translation_rationale': 'The term \u3161\u3136\u3163\u312b \u3092\u3135\u314d \u314c\u316a is a direct translation of the English phrase "Digital Cultural Heritage". However, I have modified it to make it more native-sounding in Korean. The word \u3161\u3136\u3163\u312b (dugi) means "culture" or "heritage", and \u3092\u3135\u314d \u314c\u316a (gudae) is a compound of \u3092 (ga), meaning "to save" or "to preserve", and \u314c\u316a (mu), which can be interpreted as "digital" or "information". The resulting term, \u3161\u3136\u3163\u312b \u3092\u3135\u314d \u314c\u316a, conveys a sense of digital preservation and conservation of cultural heritage. Alternative terms may include \u3130\u3137\u314b\u3131 \u3092\u3135\u314d \u314c\u316a (deulgigeol gudeung), which uses the term "digital" explicitly, or \u3163\u312f \u314e\u313f \u3134\u314d \u314c\u316a (\u3151\u3148 \u3087\u314b\u3131), which incorporates a more abstract concept of "cultural asset".', 
'alternatives': ['\u3130\u3137\u314b\u3131 \u3092\u3135\u314d \u314c\u316a (deulgigeol gudeung)', '\u3151\u3148 \u3087\u314b\u3131 (mujeong gudeung)', '\u3163\u312f \u314e\u313f \u3134\u314d \u314c\u316a (\u3151\u3148 \u3087\u314b\u3131)']}

{'translated_term': 'ડિજીટલ સાંસ્કૃતિક વારસ', 'translation_rationale': 'I used the term "ડિજીટલ" which is a loanword from English, and "સાંસ્કૃતિક" to convey the meaning of cultural heritage. The prefix "ડિજીટલ" is commonly used in Kashmiri to denote something related to technology or digital. I combined it with "વારસ", which means "heritage" or "legacy", to create a term that represents the digital preservation of cultural heritage.'}

Alternative translation: 'ડિજીટલ ઇતિહાસ' (Digital Itihas) - This alternative uses the term "ઇતિહાસ" to convey the meaning of history or legacy, which is closely related to cultural heritage.

{'translated_term': 'ડિજીટલ ઇતિહાસ', 'translation_rationale': 'This alternative translation uses a term that conveys the idea of digital preservation and historical significance.'}

{'translated_term': '\u0428\u0430\u043d\u0430\u0442\u045b\u0440\u0438\u043f\u0442\u0438\u043a \t\u0441\u043e\u0442\u0441\u0435\u0442\u043c\u0435\u043c\u0430\u0449 \u043c\u0441 \u043c\u0443\u0447\u044b', 'translation_rationale': 'The term "Digital Cultural Heritage" is translated as "" (shanariatipistik masiyat), which emphasizes the digital aspect of cultural heritage, emphasizing the importance of preserving and presenting the culture through new media. This translation maintains a strong connection to the Kyrgyz language while accurately conveying the concept.'}

Alternative translation: 
{'translated_term': '\u0441\u0430\u043d\u0430\u0442\u045b\u0440\u0438\u043f\u0442\u0438\u043C \t\u043c\u0441 \u043c\u0441 \u043f\u0445\u043b\u0438\u0449\u0430\u0444\u0442 \u043c\u0443\u0447\u044e', 'translation_rationale': This alternative translation uses the word "" (sanariatipistik masiry) instead of "\u0428\u0430\u043d\u0430\u0442\u045b\u0449\u0438\u043f\u0442\u0438\u043a \t\u0441\u043e\u0442\u0441\u0435\u0444\u0445\u0442 \u043c\u0441" which is more common in Kyrgyz language. This translation uses the word "\u0441\u0430\u043d\u0430\u0442\u045b\u0449\u0438\u043f\u0442\u0438\u043a" (sanaripitiik) which means "digital" to convey the digital aspect of cultural heritage.'}

{'translated_term': '\u0428\u0430\u043d\u0430\u0442\u045b\u0440\u0438\u043f\u0442\u0438\u0439 \t\u0441\u043e\u0444\u0443\u0447 \u043c\u0441 \u043c\u0441 \u044c\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0444\u0440\u0430\u0446\u0438', 'translation_rationale': This translation uses the word "\u0428\u0430\u043d\u0430\u0442\u045b\u0449\u0438\u043f\u0442\u0438\u043a" (shanariatipitiik) which is more formal and commonly used in Kyrgyz language. The word "\u0441\u043e\u0444\u0443\u0447 \u043c\u0441" (soorash mas) means "preservation of cultural heritage", conveying the importance of preserving cultural assets.'}

{'translated_term': 'Hereditas Culturalis Digitalis', 
 'translation_rationale': 'The phrase "Digital Cultural Heritage" is a combination of two concepts: digital, referring to the digital realm and cultural heritage, referring to intangible aspects of a culture. The Latin term "Hereditas" conveys the idea of inheritance or legacy, which suits well with the concept of cultural heritage. Adding the adjective "Culturalis" clarifies that it refers specifically to cultural aspects, while "Digitalis" emphasizes the digital nature of this heritage.', 
 'alternatives': ['Hereditas Informatica', 'Patrimonium Culturale Digitale']}

{'translated_term': 'Obusika bwobujjala bw&#39;obuwangwa obwa digito', 
 'translation_rationale': 'I used the term "Bujjala" which means "digital" in Luganda, instead of Google Translate's suggestion "Digito" to maintain a more culturally sensitive and precise translation. The term "Obusika bwobuwangwa" is already present in Luganda language, so I kept it as it is, meaning "cultural heritage". The prefix "bwa-" is also used to indicate something related to or characteristic of the thing that follows, which is appropriate for this context.', 
 'alternative_translations': ['Obusika bwobujjala obwa kibuka', alternative term suggesting a more straightforward translation without using the existing Luganda term "Buwangwa"]}

{'translated_term': '\u0444\u043e\u0442\u0438\u0431\u0430\u043b\u0435\u043d\u0438 \kult\u035be paveldas', 'translation_rationale': 'I used the phrase &quot;Skaitmeninių kultūros paveldų&quot; as a starting point, but then modified it to &quot;Digitalinė kultūros paveldas&quot; to better convey the meaning of Digital Cultural Heritage. The term "digitalinė" is more suitable in Lithuanian, emphasizing the digital aspect, whereas "skaitmeninis" implies something related to information or data transfer (though it can still be used). The phrase &quot;Digital Cultural Heritage&quot; is more idiomatic and straightforward, so I preferred to use that term for translation.'}

Alternative translations:
- {'translated_term': '\u0444\u043e\u0442\u0438\u0431\u0430l\u0435\u043d\u0449\u0438\u043e \kult\u035be paveldas', 'translation_rationale': 'Using &quot;Digitalinis kultūros paveldas&quot; instead of &quot;Skaitmeninių kultūros paveldų&quot;, I emphasized the word "digitalinis" to make it clear that the term refers specifically to digital aspects. This phrase may sound more modern and precise in Lithuanian.'

